BAR Droid phone version of BAR's Widget Selector (luaui/widgets/widget_selector.lua): its "Cost" column off at every start.
With the column on (BAR's default, saved on), the selector keeps BAR's widget profiler running all game whether the panel
is open or not (luaui/Include/widget_profiling.lua): every call-in of every widget wrapped, each call reading the timer
and Lua's memory counter twice, hundreds of calls a frame. On the dev phone in a late 16-player game that is spread over
every widget's time (docs/ENGINE-SIM.md on engine/sim, "BAR's Lua on phones"). The column can still be switched on in
the panel for the rest of the game. Since BAR test-31958 the switch lives in luaui/Include/widget_selector/model.lua,
which the engine's phone versions do not reach: the widget turns off the model's shared filters after the model loads
and after it reads the saved config. And the panel no wider than the screen (docs/upstream/bar-windows-upright.patch,
written for BAR: upright it was about twice the screen's width). Applied by the engine (BarDroidPhoneLuaDir) to BAR's
file as LuaUI loads it; if a block finds no place, BAR's own file runs.

@@@ find
local fav, filters, deps = model.fav, model.filters, model.deps
@@@ with
local fav, filters, deps = model.fav, model.filters, model.deps
filters.profiler = false -- BAR Droid (phone): the Cost column off at every start (the model's default: on)
@@@ end

@@@ find
function widget:SetConfigData(data)
	model.setConfigData(data)
end
@@@ with
function widget:SetConfigData(data)
	model.setConfigData(data)
	filters.profiler, filters.byLoad = false, false -- BAR Droid (phone): off at every start, whatever was saved
end
@@@ end

@@@ find
local widgetScale = (vsy / 1080)
@@@ with
local widgetScale = math.min(vsy / 1080, vsx / (screenWidthOrg + 50)) -- BAR Droid (phone; docs/upstream/bar-windows-upright.patch): no wider than the screen
@@@ end

@@@ find
	widgetScale = (vsy / 1080)
@@@ with
	widgetScale = math.min(vsy / 1080, vsx / (screenWidthOrg + 50)) -- BAR Droid (phone): no wider than the screen
@@@ end
